    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1301">

                <pb facs="1129" n="815" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg815"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 855.48/29</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-07">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 7, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>590. Belgian Commission requests that you secure from German Government
                    unmolested passage for neutral food ships from United <pb facs="1130" n="816"
                        xml:id="pg816"/> States to Holland for Belgium. This has been done by
                    British Government.</p>
                <p>Also inform Department whether German Government has placed embargo on
                    importation into Belgium, in neutral ships, of thoroughly disinfected and
                    cleaned second-hand clothing.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
